Z||000000||Scott_M||12-21-2000||08:27 PM||||I've searched for other posts like this but didn't find an answer.***The EGR has two openings...a round one going to the engine, and a square one leading to the throttle. My situation is...the square opening to the throttle is burn't & blackened inside.Also, near the round opening towards the front, the gasket has been "eaten through" pretty much all the way.  Is that normal? If not what could I do to fix it? AND..could this be the reason it didn't pass the SMOG check?<BR> ||||reg||9
Z||000001||deceler8||12-22-2000||12:40 PM||||Gasket burn through probably means nothing more than the valve has been loose, and the exhaust gas burned out a corner of it.<P>It may be time for a new EGR, especially if you didn't pass smog. At the cery least, you need to put on a new EGR gasket.<P>As to the passages being blackened...pretty normal. The system recycles uncatalyzed exhaust, so it will leave carbon deposits, especially if you don't drive a lot. A whole lot of carbon is probably from a bad oxygen sensor or bad valve seals...bad valve seals will also cause the blue smoke at startup.||||reg||1
